        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2025/11/Apple-generates-2.4-million-per-employee-but-is-only-third-in-the-ranking.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple and the Department of Justice have submitted a joint notice of impasse over how recent Apple’s documents must be to fall within the scope of discovery in their ongoing antitrust lawsuit. Here are the details.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"aapl\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1075255\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/21/apple-and-doj-notify-court-of-impasse-over-document-cutoff-in-antitrust-lawsuit/#more-1075255\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
        "type": "Technology",
        "source": "9to5Mac"
